      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to -5}\\frac{4x}{x+1}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule for limits, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -5}\\frac{4x}{x+1} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -5}4x}{{lim}_{x\\to -5}(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(-5)}{-5+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{-4} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
