      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{1-{x}^{3}}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule for limits, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{1-{x}^{3}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to -1}({x}^{2}-4)}{{lim}_{x\\to -1}(1-{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}-4}{1-(-1)^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
